    "finalText": "Everything is in place and verified. Final state of the delivery:\n\n**Implementation** (`/workspace`):\n- `internal/api` — chi v5.2.1 routes: `POST /links` (201 create, 409 duplicate, 422 validation), `GET /links` (ascending list with `items`/`total`), `GET /links/{code}`, `GET /r/{code}` (302 + exact `Location`, clicks incremented atomically via `UPDATE … RETURNING`), JSON `{\"error\": …}` bodies on all failures\n- `internal/store` — pgx v5.7.5 over `database/sql` (idiomatic Go persistence), reads `DATABASE_URL`, no hard-coded credentials\n- `cmd/migrate` — applies pending `migrations/*.sql`, tracked in `schema_migrations`\n- `start.sh` — runs migrations, then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` (no dependency installs)\n- `README.md` — \"Starting the server\" section plus API reference\n\n**Verification** — a 34-check curl battery passed (validation edge cases including 21-char and non-ASCII codes, duplicate 409, URL echo exactness with query/fragment, click increments of exactly 1 per redirect). I also killed and restarted the server and confirmed data and click counts survived, and did a fully cold start from an empty database. The DB has been reset afterward so the automated suite starts clean, and all background processes are stopped.\n\nOne note: pgx latest (v5.13) requires Go 1.25, so I pinned v5.7.5, the newest release compatible with the project's Go 1.24.3 toolchain."
